Delete cache entries written by a different siloscan build

Usage: siloscan cache prune [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          Scan root whose cache entries are pruned

          The path names the tree, not the cache: entries are keyed by scan root, so this says whose cache to sweep, and the cache itself is found the way a scan of that root would find it.

          [default: .]

Options:
      --cache-dir <DIR>
          Prune under DIR instead of this user's cache directory; use the same value the scans being pruned were run with

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
